    <l n="1" para="true">de puerorum deliciis, &amp; nimiâ paren-</l>
    <l n="2">tum erga liberos indulgentiâ. Sed &amp;</l>
    <l n="3">fond, stultus; fondnesse, stultitia, a-</l>
    <l n="4">mentia: nempe, <i>Quia mollis illa educa-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>tio, quam indulgentiam vocamus, ner-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>vos omnes &amp; mentis &amp; corporis frangit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">Quintiliani sunt verba: sed Germano-</l>
    <l n="8">rum eam fuisse sententiam, ex educa-</l>
    <l n="9">tionis ratione liquet. Tacit: <i>Dominum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>ac servum nullis educationis deliciis dig-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>noscas.</i> Reliqua apud ipsum leguntur.</l>
    <l n="12" para="true">'Ἐρυθρὸς, ruber, red.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">'Ἔαρ, ἔαρος, ver. Angl. peare, (Germ.</l>
    <l n="14">jar.) annus: quòd à vere annum multi</l>
    <l n="15">aufpicarentur.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">'Εἰμί, fum, I am.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">'Ἐλπίς, spes, hope; an &amp; to helpe, cùm</l>
    <l n="18">spes &amp; præsidium sint affinia?</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">'Ἑλκω, trahere, to hale.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">'Ἐϋω, inflammare, torrere, to sindge.</l>
    <l n="21">De aspiratione in f. vertente, vide supra.</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">'Ἑστιάω, convivio excipere: ἑστιάτωρ,</l>
    <l n="23">conviva: Angl. a gueft.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">Εἰδω, Præter. οἶδα, novi, scio: Angl. wote: ἐκ οἶδα, I wote not.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Εἰδὼ, φρόνησις (Hesychio) prudentia:</l>
    <l n="26">εἰδὼς, sciens, peritus, witt, wittie.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">'Ἐγχλιώσιν,</l>
